  "issue_records": [
    {
      "number": 1075,
      "url": "https://github.com/Nemocas/AbstractAlgebra.jl/issues/1075",
      "state": "closed",
      "title": "Poly sqrt test failure",
      "closed": true,
      "defect_evidence": true,
      "is_pull_request": false,
      "labels": [],
      "body_excerpt": "The following very rare issue seems to occur randomly.\r\n\r\n```\r\njulia> S, x = PolynomialRing(QQ, \"x\")\r\n(Univariate Polynomial Ring in x over Rationals, x)\r\n\r\njulia> f = x^2 + x + 1//4\r\nx^2 + x + 1//4\r\n\r\njulia> issquare_with_sqrt(f)\r\n(true, x + 1//2)\r\n\r\njulia> issquare(f)\r\nfalse\r\n\r\njulia> issquare_with_sqrt(f)\r\n(false, 0)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe following may be related, but I only seem to be able to trigger it for longer polynomials (length >= 20)\r\n\r\n```\r\njulia> S, x = PolynomialRing(QQ, \"x\")\r\n(Univariate Polynomial Ring in x over Rationals, x)\r\n\r\njulia> f = -1//8*x^17 - 11//16*x^16 + 1//2*x^15 - 1//3*x^14 + 4//3*x^13 + 3//5*x^12 + 5//4*x^11 - 7//15*x^10 + 1//5*x^9 + 1//4*x^8 + 1//3*x^7 - 2*x^6 + 8//3*x^5 + 14*x^4 - x^2 + 9//2*x - 2//7\r\n-1//8*x^17 - 11//16*x^16 + 1//2*x^15 - 1//3*x^14 + 4//3*x^13 + 3//5*x^12 + 5//4*x^11 - 7//15*x^10 + 1//5*x^9 + 1//4*x^8 + 1//3*x^7 - 2*x^6 + 8//3*x^5 + 14*x^4 - x^2 + 9//2*x - 2//7\r\n\r\njulia> issquare(f^2)\r\nfalse\r\n```\r\n"
    },
    {
      "number": 1077,
      "url": "https://github.com/Nemocas/AbstractAlgebra.jl/issues/1077",
      "state": "closed",
      "title": "Very serious bug",
      "closed": true,
      "defect_evidence": true,
      "is_pull_request": false,
      "labels": [],
      "body_excerpt": "This is with Julia 1.6.2:\r\n\r\n```\r\njulia> using AbstractAlgebra\r\n\r\njulia> S, x = PolynomialRing(QQ, \"x\")\r\n(Univariate Polynomial Ring in x over Rationals, x)\r\n\r\njulia> f = S(1//2)\r\n1//2\r\n\r\njulia> c = coeff(f, 0)\r\n1//2\r\n\r\njulia> d = -c\r\n-1//2\r\n\r\njulia> mul!(d, d, d)\r\n1//4\r\n\r\njulia> c\r\n1//4\r\n```\r\n\r\nI have no idea what is going on here. It seems to only happen when I pull the rational value from the polynomial.\r\n\r\nThis is the cause of the first issue in #1075"
    },
    {
      "number": 1078,
      "url": "https://github.com/Nemocas/AbstractAlgebra.jl/pull/1078",
      "state": "closed",
      "title": "Remove mutation for julia types",
      "closed": true,
      "defect_evidence": false,
      "is_pull_request": true,
      "labels": [],
      "body_excerpt": "Fixes #1077 \r\nFixes #1075 (both issues)\r\n\r\nTurning off mutation for Julia types appears to be necessary for correctness (see #1077), as Julia doesn't make the same assumptions as us that new objects are created that don't alias even in part when arithmetic operations are performed, e.g. \"-a\" for a Rational{BigInt} keeps the same denominator identically.\r\n\r\n Test code now takes about 9 minutes to run, which seems acceptable."
    }
  ],
